| SCN-042 | T-011 | Human uses Tab/Enter/Space, comment editing, source controls, narrow/wide native views and down/up scroll for every registered locale | Meaningful focus/readable context stable with no observed content/focus jump or flicker; typing/default selection alone cannot approve | evidence/NATIVE_ACCESSIBILITY.md |
| SCN-043 | T-011 | Human closes inline and large view; observe UI lifecycle, backend close/expiry and rejected subsequent calls independently | View closure undecided; actual backend teardown/session_expired evidence recorded; tab closure alone never substitutes for teardown | evidence/NATIVE_TEARDOWN.json |
| SCN-044 | T-012 | Execute fixed before/after lifecycle corpus with same or explicitly separated model/runtime/host conditions | Zero routine undocumented invocation/parser searches and control-table hand-edits, no false next-step or weakened negative protections; observed metrics retained; protected foreign/reference hashes unchanged | evidence/FLOW_BENEFIT.json |
| SCN-045 | T-012 | Review actual diff/task fulfillment/structure and aggregate criterion/decision/scenario evidence including gaps | Required reviews have actual outcomes/current binding; qa-gate alone decides pass/revise/block, native gap or whole-flow contradiction prevents pass | evidence/QA_INDEX.json |

### 3.2 Execution and evidence rules

1. T-001 captures commit and tracked/untracked/index baseline separately, exact protected source hashes, active shared-owner scope, installed/runtime/resource identities and the two completed reference collections. Preserve the already authorized early-UR Core changes as baseline delta, not newly implemented work. Read-only before corpus includes the observed shortened-writer versus full-reader UX/PRD and completed/open-OR contradictions. Baseline fixtures are copied/hashed to disposable roots before any test writes.
2. Run changed owner tests first, then required Core/CLI/MCP/UI package checks through the existing package scripts found during approved-TP preparation. Record exact commands, exit codes, environment and source/build digests in evidence/COMMANDS.json; no invented passing command names or broad repeated checks without change/failure. Extend existing state/dispatch/recording/approval/revision/closeout/transport/UI suites before adding an isolated new harness. A needed new scenario belongs to the same owner's test area, not a second policy implementation.
3. WRITE_REPLAY_MATRIX covers presentation, approval, internal/evidence, reviewed artefact, non-approval, early PRD reopen, early UR/late source apply/recovery, and structured/Quick closeout. Revision preview/apply share their own existing identity; cross-family UUID collisions reject. Store per-case operation/payload digest, pre/post revision, canonical receipt and separately current observation. Failure/recovery adds explicit origin and direction, never inferred idempotence.
4. PERSISTENCE_CHECKPOINTS/EARLY_UR_RECOVERY/CLOSEOUT_RECOVERY enumerate each actually introduced or retained checkpoint before qualifying its family. Inject exceptions/process loss before and after durable intent, staging/archive publication, each owned output publication, Run atomic rename, backlog rename, final checks and journal retirement. Assert exact old/new hashes, seal, receipt count, pending state and recovery outcome. Test malformed journals, unsafe paths, source interference and concurrent shared backlog ownership. Do not claim multi-file atomicity, native Windows durability or power-loss behavior from synthetic process failure.
5. Record consumed PRD/SD/TP/result versions and current/history/unknown evidence associations. Missing binding remains unknown; an unstructured first row never wins by position. Parent context obligations and accepted-open dispositions follow existing completion rules; no foreign/parent closeout is simulated as authorized live work.
6. Build one reproducible candidate from the approved implementation. CANDIDATE_IDENTITY names source commit/delta, build output/package/runtime/resource digests, dependency/tool versions and actual served producer. Rebuild after any source change that affects qualified behavior and rerun affected tests/native observations. Generated-file/runtime propagation uses existing owners. No automatic installation/restart is permitted by this plan: prepare the candidate and a concise exact loading/observation action for the user. Unloaded or differing served code remains a qualification gap.
7. Native evidence never comes from browser mocks, UI automation-generated approval, model text, API approval configuration or capability advertisement alone. Source/build/protocol/browser/native classes are marked separately. The app-only facade and text path retain cooperative_local assurance; tests establish supported behavior, not independent gesture identity. Actual host denial/confirmation must be observed where the host supports them; unavailable required mediation blocks click qualification rather than being reported as a pass.
8. Locale rendering and native accessibility matrices enumerate all registered languages from the canonical locale registry at preparation, retaining the exact list and candidate. Include inline and larger views, read/comment/action, pending/uncertain/blocked/stale/expired/history/recovery messages, exact labels and source-language distinction. A missing locale/native observation is explicit missing evidence; mere key completeness is insufficient.
9. QA_INDEX links each actual scenario result and source set, with pass/fail/not observed and precise gaps. Required Task Plan Review, Clean Implementation Review and Code Review assess actual task fulfillment, structure and diff, respectively. Only qa-gate decides final pass/revise/block. Passing authoring readiness, a built candidate or earlier bootstrap does not satisfy QA.

### 3.3 Prepared native Codex sequence

Use disposable targets and deliberate human test decisions; the live Run's QA/UAT approval remains separate. Keep one exact served candidate loaded throughout each sequence and retain the resource/runtime/session identity and backend receipt/proof alongside the user's bounded observation.

- First show the inline focused decision card for an eligible exact gate. Read title/version/full summary, change comparison or its absence, open points and consequence. Open the exact larger document, inspect provenance/source controls and return. Discuss in chat before deciding; confirm no decision occurred from reading or AI response.
- On separate eligible test presentations, the human clicks Freigeben, enters a concrete comment and chooses Änderung wünschen, and chooses Ablehnen. Inspect registered outcome, source/version, one receipt and current owner. Demonstrate later exact human Approval text on a still-current presentation; demonstrate rejection of old/quoted/foreign text by contract tests rather than asking the user to approve wrong production material.
- Observe actual host execution consent without presenting it as another gate. Test supported deny then valid retry without inventing a second business decision. Observe pending and a controlled lost acknowledgement: resolve original operation status before resubmitting. App-only unsupported host behavior stays blocked with an honest fallback and evidence gap.
- Per registered language, use Tab/Enter/Space on explicit actions and document/source controls; type into the comment, resize the native sidebar narrow and wide, scroll down/back and return between views. Record actual focus/content stability and readable complete labels. Input-field Enter or default/preselection must not approve.
- Close the inline card and large view; independently inspect actual ui lifecycle/backend close or expiry and rejected later session calls. Tab closure alone is not proof. Source change/refresh/late results must not revive the old action; a still-current text presentation has its own eligibility.

The agent prepares the actual test version, actions and evidence capture before asking for a human step. User replies report only what was actually observed; do not transfer earlier “stable/no flicker” evidence from another candidate. If host-native steps cannot be observed, list them as missing and keep QA from claiming complete acceptance.

### 3.4 Benefit and stop conditions

Retain a fixed corpus: no-source-revision structured chain, revised-source+completed-UX renewed chain, supported recording/approval including click/text conflict, early UR-at-SD renewal, lost-acknowledgement/recovery, structured and Quick closeout, current/history evidence inspection. Compare same scenarios and conditions before/after; separate changed host/model conditions. Count routine undocumented invocation/parser searches, manual control-table edits, invalid schema attempts, false next-step statements, redundant continuation/business prompts and successful recovery. Necessary engineering reads, deliberate gates and external native actions are separately classified, not hidden as zero work. Claim weaker-model improvement only with an actual bound model comparison; deterministic improvement alone is a workflow result.

No partial success is whole-run pass. A consumer inconsistency, widened authority, invented history, duplicate effect, unowned journal path, schema-budget failure, missing current binding, foreign modification or absent required native/locale evidence requires owner remediation and qa-gate revise/block. A preparation finding that contradicts approved architecture/budget/reuse goes through the existing SD/source revision owner before implementation; do not improvise an adapter fix or silently shrink scope.

## 4. Brownfield Scope

After TP approval, inspect the exact dirty baseline and current shared active scopes through existing control owners, then record actual implementation-preparation Brownfield Analysis. Known reused paths below are touchpoints, not a license to modify every listed file:

- Core state/evaluation: control-evaluation/run-state.js, gate-policy.js, gate-check.js, next-action.js; control-state/run-step-policy.js; skill-dispatch/service.js. Trace shortened preparations and executable prose branches once, replacing them through approved shared ownership.
- Core command/recording/authority: createCoreServices/index and existing command contracts; run-steps.js, run-artefact-recording.js, artefact-binding-proof.js, artefact-bindings.js, run-presentation.js, approval-command.js, approval-operations.js. Add proposed decision contracts only at their resolved owners.
- Revision/durability: run-revision-boundary.js, run-revision.js, run-source-revisions.js, run-revision-history.js, run-step-transaction.js, run-state-writer.js and run-backlog-writer.js. Preserve current early-UR bootstrap delta/archive, old journal readers, append-only guards and Run-before-Backlog lock order.
- Evidence/read semantics: traceability-readiness.js, run-presentation-render.js, run-work-summary.js and existing evidence/cockpit/document proof owners. Keep canonical text digest distinct from raw document proof and preserve unknown historic applicability.
- Transport/UI/package: CLI owner validation and mcp-dispatch-runtime.js; mcp-server server/worker/worker-entry/ui-capability; control-ui App/state/DocumentView/RunDocuments and mcp transport/EmbeddedEntry; existing cockpit-session and resource/capability ownership; existing generation/package/integrity scripts and registered locales.
- Repository instructions/architecture: applicable AGENTS and declared normative docs/architecture/03-agentenkontrolle-zielbild.md with OP/R references; exact current contracts and approved source maps. Resolve a real precedence/overlap conflict before touching code, without assuming a new worktree copies uncommitted approved baseline.

The additional MCP-candidate assignment remains active. Log routine invocation/format discoveries or direct Core helper calls in MCP_CANDIDATES.md with user purpose, actual gap versus existing capability, owner, exact binding/input/result and priority. Ordinary source review or an installation mismatch does not justify another endpoint. This plan creates no memory updates.

## 5. Out Of Scope

No universal code-search/discovery service, general cockpit writer, second policy/parser/approval ledger, remote authentication/deployment, independent human-origin enforcement, general lifecycle widening, foreign Run reconciliation, automatic installer/restart, release publication or Git action. No code changes before TP approval and actual required preparation. No retrospective QA, artificial legacy associations, transferred historical approvals or inferred native evidence. The unrelated gate-decision-card Run is not selected or modified.

## 6. Risks And Blockers

The main risks are expanding a shared owner with inconsistent consumers, old executing-runtime compatibility, ambiguous crash commit points, session-versus-human-origin overclaim, decision guard circumvention by a fresh envelope, and missing actual Codex permission/accessibility/localized evidence. Mitigations are the approved shared owners, per-family/phase tests, exact receipts/current observations, rejected-version guard, separate evidence classes and explicit QA gaps.

Plan architecture is fixed by approved SD; only execution/test detail is supplied here. All 21 PRD criteria and all 18 SD decisions map to declared tasks/scenarios. Technical budget/reuse contradiction, new material authority or source-intent change must return to the existing revision owner. There is no accepted-debt exception or fallback-as-native-pass. If the current dirty baseline or installation differs, rebind/qualify the precise candidate rather than attributing an old observation to it.

## 7. Next Step

Check authoring readiness and semantic derivation; register TP derived_from the exact approved SD with a fresh reviewed mapping/input and obtain a new bound presentation. Wait for deliberate Approval: TP. After approval, record actual implementation-preparation Brownfield Analysis, then implement/test only if canonical permission allows. Required reviews and QA occur from actual current results; QA/UAT remain separate human decisions. Git handoff needs its own request.

## AGDF Approval Summary (de; source=en)

- Ziel: Den freigegebenen gemeinsamen Core-/MCP-Ablauf einschließlich Entscheidungskarte in einem Run umsetzen und vollständig prüfen. Der Plan verbindet alle 21 PRD-Kriterien und 18 SD-Entscheidungen mit 12 abhängigen Aufgaben und 45 konkreten Prüfszenarien. Noch keine Umsetzung oder QA.
- Umfang und Reihenfolge: Nach TP-Freigabe zuerst tatsächliche Brownfield-Vorbereitung und geschützte Baseline. Dann gemeinsamer Zustand/Folgeschritt, begrenzte Verträge und Erfassung/Recovery, Freigabe/Nichtfreigabe/Konkurrenz, Quellenrevision, Abschluss/Evidenz, CLI/MCP und Karte. Anschließend exakten Kandidaten, native Codex-Bedienung, Gesamtfluss und Reviews prüfen. Einzelne Etappen erfüllen nicht den gesamten Run.
- Kernprüfungen: Vollständiger Leser und Writer müssen denselben Stand liefern, auch nach UR-Revision mit erledigter UX. Anzeigetext darf keine Ausführung steuern. Autorenformate, Schemas, Quellenbeziehungen, Seals und fünf Werkzeuggruppen samt App-only-Fassade müssen übereinstimmen; fremde/deaktivierte Actions bleiben gesperrt und die SD-Budgets werden gemessen.
- Freigaben: Präsentation allein bleibt unentschieden. Tatsächlicher neuer Text und bewusster Klick nutzen dieselbe Freigabeautorität; Fragen, Zitate, alte/fremde Antworten, KI-Aussagen und Tool-Erlaubnis entscheiden nicht. Änderung mit Kommentar und Ablehnung erhalten eigene Nichtfreigabe-Belege. Unverändert abgelehntes Material kann nicht durch eine neue Präsentationshülle freigegeben werden; neue Fassung benötigt neue Entscheidung.
- Konkurrenz und Recovery: Jede Schreibfamilie prüft identische Wiederholung, veränderte Nutzlast, UUID-Konflikt, verlorene Antwort und Konkurrenz. Doppelklick, verschiedene Vorgangskennungen und gleichzeitiger Text/Klick erzeugen höchstens einen Effekt. An allen tatsächlichen Archiv-/Ausgabe-/Run-/Backlog-Grenzen werden Abbruch und Recovery geprüft: vor Run-Commit eigene Ausgaben zurücksetzen, danach fertigstellen. Alte Journale bleiben beim vorhandenen Owner; keine behauptete Mehrdatei-Atomizität.
- Quellenrevision und Abschluss: Bestehende frühe PRD-/späte CD+Tests-Wege und begrenzte UR-Wiederöffnung bei SD werden über Core/CLI/echtes MCP samt Negativ- und Abbruchfällen geprüft. Der echte bereits ausgeführte Revisionsfall bleibt lesender Historiennachweis. Erneuerte Analysen/Freigaben müssen dieselbe Run-Kette fortsetzen. Beide strukturierten Modi und Quick Task müssen OR, Lebenszyklus und Backlog konsistent abschließen; fehlende Pflichten blockieren. Kein Git wird ausgeführt.
- Evidenz und Kompatibilität: Aktuelle exakt gebundene QA-/UAT-Nachweise, ersetzte Historie und unbekannte Zuordnung bleiben getrennt. Bestehende Dokument-/Entwurfsprüfung, fremde Quellen/Freigaben, Run-Version und alte lesbare Belege werden geschützt. Alte ausführende Versionen erhalten keine neue Qualifikation. Schreibfähigkeiten lassen sich deaktivieren, ohne gespeicherte Effekte zu löschen.
- Tatsächliche Codex-Prüfung: Einen exakt erzeugten und bewusst geladenen Kandidaten mit Paket-/Runtime-/Ressourcenkennung prüfen. Der Nutzer liest die kleine Karte, öffnet die exakte große Dokumentansicht, kehrt zurück und diskutiert. Auf getrennten Testfassungen erfolgen Freigeben, Änderungswunsch mit Kommentar, Ablehnen und späterer exakter Text. Zusätzlich echte Host-Erlaubnis/Ablehnung, Tastatur/Fokus, schmale/breite Ansicht, Scrollen und alle registrierten Sprachen beobachten. Ansichtsende und Backend-Teardown werden getrennt belegt.
- Prüfgrenzen: Synthetische Entscheidungen dienen nur isolierten Tests; sie erteilen keine Live-Freigabe. Browser-/Quellen-/Build-/Protokollnachweise ersetzen keine native Nutzeraktion. Sitzungsschlüssel und App-only-Metadaten beweisen keine unabhängige menschliche Herkunft. Fehlende Host-Unterstützung oder Beobachtung bleibt offen und verhindert vollständige Klickqualifikation; Textfallback ist kein Ersatz. Installation/Neustart erfolgt nicht automatisch.
- Nutzen und Zusatzauftrag: Ein fester Vorher-/Nachher-Korpus zählt Routine-Suche, Handedits, Schemafehler, falsche Folgeschritte, unnötige Aufforderungen und Recovery. Ziel sind null undokumentierte Routine-Aufruf-/Parser-Suchen, null Kontrolltabellen-Handedits und keine falschen Folgeangaben bei erhaltenen Kontrollen. Notwendige technische Recherche, fachliche Entscheidungen und externe Nutzeraktionen bleiben separat sichtbar. MCP-Kandidaten werden weiter dokumentiert; Nutzen für schwächere Modelle wird nur bei tatsächlicher Modellmessung behauptet.
- Risiken und Abschluss: Widerspruch zu freigegebener Architektur/Wiederverwendung/Budget verlangt vorherige Revision, keine Einzelkorrektur außerhalb des Konzepts. Echte TP-/Struktur-/Code-Reviews und ein konkreter Nachweisindex gehen an qa-gate; nur dort wird pass/revise/block entschieden. Fehlende native/langabhängige Evidenz, doppelte Effekte, widersprüchliche Verbraucher oder beschädigte Bindungen verhindern Pass. QA/UAT und Git-Handoff bleiben eigene Entscheidungen/Aufträge.
- Nächster Schritt: Mit Approval: TP diesen Aufgaben-/Testplan freigeben, Änderung verlangen oder ablehnen. Die Freigabe erlaubt zuerst die notwendige Implementierungsvorbereitung und danach die im Plan gebundene Umsetzung, soweit der aktuelle Core sie erlaubt.
